---
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";

// Operator: Idris Idriszade, sole proprietor, Texas. No postal address is
// published: email only.
//
// Contact is hello@gatewerk.com, already the site's published address. See the
// note in privacy.astro for why that rather than a new privacy@ alias.
//
// Governing law is Texas, United States, matching the operator's location.
//
// Checked against the source:
//   - Self hosting is unrestricted and carries no plan gate. There is no licence
//     check in the codebase and no seat limit in the OSS product.
//   - Billing is behind BILLING_WAITLIST and nobody is charged at launch, so the
//     payment section describes a trial that cannot silently convert.
//   - Account deletion works for both password and Supabase accounts.
// The liability wording is deliberately plain rather than shouty.
const updated = "2 August 2026";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Terms · Gatewerk"
  description="The terms for using gatewerk.com and the hosted service. Self-hosting is governed by the licence, not by these terms."
>
  <div style="position:absolute;top:-260px;left:50%;transform:translateX(-50%);width:1100px;height:600px;background:radial-gradient(ellipse at center,rgba(33,181,113,.1),transparent 68%);pointer-events:none;filter:blur(20px);z-index:0;"></div>

  <section style="position:relative;z-index:1;max-width:820px;margin:0 auto;padding:84px 32px 96px;">

    <h1 class="gw-up gw-display" style="font-weight:600;font-size:clamp(34px,5vw,48px);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-.03em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:0;">Terms</h1>
    <p class="gw-up" style="max-width:640px;margin:22px 0 0;font-size:17px;line-height:1.6;color:#b4b4ac;text-wrap:pretty;">
      These terms cover the website and the hosted service. If you self host, your rights
      come from the licence instead, and they are broader than anything here.
    </p>
    <p class="gw-up gw-mono" style="margin:20px 0 0;font-size:11.5px;letter-spacing:.06em;color:#7b7b72;">
      LAST UPDATED {updated}
    </p>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">Who you are agreeing with</h2>
    <p style="max-width:640px;margin:18px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#b4b4ac;">
      Gatewerk is operated by <strong style="color:#e4e0d6;">Idris Idriszade</strong>,
      an individual trading as a sole proprietor in Texas, United States. In these terms that
      person is "we". Reach us at <a href="mailto:hello@gatewerk.com" style="color:#3fca8a;text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(63,202,138,.35);">hello@gatewerk.com</a>.
    </p>

    <div style="border:1px solid rgba(33,181,113,.24);background:rgba(33,181,113,.06);border-radius:14px;padding:20px 22px;margin-top:26px;max-width:640px;">
      <div class="gw-mono" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.08em;color:#3fca8a;">IF YOU SELF HOST</div>
      <p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.65;color:#cfcfc5;">
        You do not need our permission and these terms do not restrict you. The server is
        AGPL-3.0, the client libraries are Apache-2.0, and there is no licence check, no seat
        limit and no paid tier inside the software. Run it for a team of one or a team of
        five hundred. See the licensing page for the detail.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">Your account</h2>
    <p style="max-width:640px;margin:18px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#b4b4ac;">
      You need to be old enough to enter a contract where you live. Keep your sign in details
      to yourself, and tell us if you think someone else has them. What happens under your
      account is your responsibility.
    </p>
    <p style="max-width:640px;margin:14px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#b4b4ac;">
      You can close your account from inside the app whenever you like. We can suspend an
      account that is being used to break the law, to attack the service, or to harm other
      people using it. If we ever do that we will tell you why.
    </p>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">Your content stays yours</h2>
    <p style="max-width:640px;margin:18px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#b4b4ac;">
      Everything you put into Gatewerk belongs to you. You give us permission to store and
      display it only so far as running the service requires. We do not use it to train
      models and we do not sell it. That permission ends when you delete the content or
      close your account.
    </p>
    <p style="max-width:640px;margin:14px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#b4b4ac;">
      You are responsible for what you put in. Do not upload things you have no right to,
      and do not use Gatewerk to break the law.
    </p>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">Paying</h2>
    <p style="max-width:640px;margin:18px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#b4b4ac;">
      Self hosting is free and always will be. The hosted service has a paid plan with a
      30 day trial that does not ask for a card. The trial does not turn into a paid
      subscription on its own: if you want to continue, you choose to.
    </p>
    <p style="max-width:640px;margin:14px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#b4b4ac;">
      Once billing is switched on, payments are handled by a third party payment processor
      and charged in advance for
      each period. You can cancel at any time and keep access until the period you paid for
      ends. If we put prices up we will give you at least 30 days notice by email.
    </p>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">What we promise, and what we do not</h2>
    <p style="max-width:640px;margin:18px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#b4b4ac;">
      We will run the hosted service with reasonable care and tell you honestly when
      something has gone wrong. We do not promise it will never be unavailable, and we do not
      offer a guaranteed uptime figure on the current plans.
    </p>
    <p style="max-width:640px;margin:14px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#b4b4ac;">
      Gatewerk is a tool for recording human decisions. It does not make decisions for you
      and it is not a substitute for your own judgement, your own legal advice or your own
      compliance obligations. A signed record shows what a person decided. It does not make
      that decision correct.
    </p>
    <p style="max-width:640px;margin:14px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#b4b4ac;">
      To the extent the law allows, the service is provided as it is, and our liability to
      you is limited to what you paid us in the twelve months before the problem arose. Some
      places do not allow limits like that, and where that is true these words do not take
      away rights you have anyway.
    </p>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">Ending it</h2>
    <p style="max-width:640px;margin:18px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#b4b4ac;">
      You can stop using the hosted service at any time. We can stop offering it, and if we
      do we will give you at least 60 days notice and a way to export your data. Since the
      software is open source, a shutdown of the hosted service does not take the product
      away from you: you can run the same thing yourself.
    </p>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">Law</h2>
    <p style="max-width:640px;margin:18px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#b4b4ac;">
      These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Texas, United States, and disputes
      go to the courts there. If you are a consumer somewhere with stronger protections, this
      does not remove them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="gw-display" style="font-size:clamp(22px,3vw,28px);font-weight:600;letter-spacing:-.02em;color:#f7f7f1;margin:56px 0 0;">Changes</h2>
    <p style="max-width:640px;margin:18px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.7;color:#b4b4ac;">
      We will post changes here and email account holders about anything significant. If you
      keep using the service after a change takes effect, that is your acceptance of it.
    </p>

  </section>
</MarketingLayout>
